{"id": "striviaqa0153", "pool": "striviaqa", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The Latin phrase you're looking for is pro bono. It means for the public good, but in practice it's used to describe professional work done voluntarily without payment, often by lawyers or doctors helping those who can't afford services.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 15, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "striviaqa0161", "pool": "striviaqa", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The three priorities were education reform, economic reform and devolution.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 6, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "striviaqa0169", "pool": "striviaqa", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The capital of Georgia is Atlanta.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 2, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "striviaqa0177", "pool": "striviaqa", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The famous person who gate crashed the state dinner for Indian President Manmohan Singh at the White House on November 2 4, 20 09 was former President Barack Obama's then- Secretary of State, Hillary Clinton. She arrived late to the event and had to make a quick entrance, which drew attention from the media.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 20, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "striviaqa0185", "pool": "striviaqa", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "He played the title character in the 1965 film of the 195 7 novel by the Russian writer Boris Pasternak, Doctor Zhivago.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 9, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "striviaqa0193", "pool": "striviaqa", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The currency of Q atar is the Qat arian riy al. It's called the Qatari riy al, and it's abbreviated as Q AR.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 8, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "striviaqa0201", "pool": "striviaqa", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "It was Mitchell Starc, who scored 85 runs for a number 11 batsman in that match.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 7, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "striviaqa0209", "pool": "striviaqa", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The king who was forced to agree to the Magna Carta was King John. He signed it in 1215 after his barons rebel led because he was being unfair and oppressive.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 9, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "striviaqa0217", "pool": "striviaqa", "n_q_chunks": 6, "onset_chunk": 5, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Anemia can be caused by a deficiency of iron. Iron is essential for making hem oglobin, the protein in red blood cells that carries oxygen throughout the body. When there's not enough iron, the body can't produce sufficient healthy red blood cells, leading to anemia.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 17, "carrier_ended": null}
